Experiment 1: Develop a program to blink 5 LEDs back and forth
Logic (Algorithm)
Step 1:Define the total number of LEDs and store their Arduino pin numbers in an array.
Step 2:Set all LED pins as OUTPUT using the setup() function.
Step 3:Inside the loop() function, execute a forward loop to glow LEDs from Pin 2 to Pin 6 one by one.
Step 4:After each LED glows for 500 ms, switch it OFF before turning ON the next LED.
Step 5:Execute a backward loop to glow LEDs from Pin 5 (LED4) to Pin 3 (LED2) one by one.
Step 6:Repeat the entire process continuously to create a running LED (Knight Rider) effect.
